From 585725146b1a792efba7a382f2acf4635fb67868 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:52:07 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] rdna-boosts: block 15: the streamed KV -- a fixed-VRAM
 resident WINDOW (Goal A) and an attendance POOL (Goal B), both opt-in

Re-based onto a691b2345 (r236)

The rung collided with everything the streamed KV binds to: the memory instances (#31141 no_alloc,
#31200 n_pad removed, #31142), the KV cache internals (#30541 on-device state copy sizes, #31073 the
rotation constants moved into a per-cache buffer, #31570 kv_rows), the Meta (tensor-split) device
(#31447) and the qwen4exp rewrite.  8 files conflicted / 12 hunks (9 expected: src/models/qwen4exp.cpp
auto-merged, the D3 residue did not conflict this time and its 59/-7 lines all landed).  A
distinctive-added-line check over the 25 auto-merged files found no dropped delivery code.

D13 (memory instances) -- re-derived, not carried:
* llama_memory_params keeps upstream's `no_alloc` and adds the delivery's `kv_pool`
  (llama-context.cpp's designated init passes both); the three `hparams.no_alloc` reads the block
  added follow #31141 out of the hparams and become the ctor's `no_alloc`.
* memory_breakdown() is re-derived over `ctxs_bufs.bufs` + `ctxs_bufs.no_alloc` instead of the old
  per-cache loop: upstream moved the no_alloc/plain accounting into llama_memory_bufs and added
  attn_rot_bufs (#31073), whose bytes are summed on top.  The pool's mirror-to-host-bucket and the
  window's resident/spill split accounting are unchanged.
* the MTP draft window's llama_kv_cache construction drops the `n_pad` argument (#31200), and the
  pool's cell count is rounded to whole PAGES (it used to round to the cache's n_pad, which no longer
  exists as a parameter -- n_ctx is unpadded now).
* create_memory() takes upstream's `params` name back (the delivery-side `params_l` rename is gone;
  the body was upstream's everywhere but two lines).
* src/llama-ext.h keeps upstream's classifier-free-guidance declaration, src/llama-memory.h keeps
  upstream's llama_memory_bufs struct, ggml-backend-meta.cpp keeps upstream's view-slab helpers next
  to ggml_backend_meta_kv_region_grow.  src/llama-context.cpp takes upstream's readback-sync hunk --
  the delivery side of it was stale F1 code (layer_inp_host_fill, deleted at R13).

D12 (quantized-KV state, rotation) -- the provider still binds at the BUFFER TYPE and no kernel
addresses cells differently: the rotation constants are a per-cache, per-layer buffer (attn_rot_bufs),
not cell-indexed, so they are outside the region; state_write/state_read keep going through the region
buffer's own copy.  Proven by the gates below, whose spilling arms really spill (16 mapping flips,
64 MiB host-backed) and whose state arm (win2mtp) takes the region path.

The r193 draft reserve is preserved (r236 absorbed the fit plumbing): common/common.cpp takes
upstream's common_fit_apply() call, and block 15's mtp_shared branch is folded into
common_draft_reserve_derive() -- the one function both `--fit` and the MoE preflight call.  Measured,
35B-A3B Q8_0 1 GPU -ncmoe 48 -c 262144 with --spec-type draft-mtp: window auto derives "draft CONTEXT
1102 MiB (kv 142 + compute 768 + slack 192)" -> arena 20527.5 MiB / 62.9 % residency; window 0 keeps
the flat 3584 MiB -> arena 17977.5 MiB / 55.1 %.  +2550 MiB of arena, +7.8 points.

Fixed on the way:
* src/llama-memory-hybrid.cpp passed its attention cache to the extended ctor positionally, so after
  upstream inserted `is_indexer` before `v_enabled` the delivery's `kv_pool` landed in `v_enabled`:
  the cache allocated NO V tensor and llama_kv_cache::cpy_v null-dereferenced on the first graph build
  (every hybrid/GDN model segfaulted at load; the dense 4B arm died before generating).  `is_indexer`
  is now named explicitly.  The other ctor call sites were audited: hybrid-idx already named it,
  model.cpp stops at `share`, and dsa/dsa-iswa/msa/dsv4 are upstream's and correct.
* ggml/src/ggml-cuda/indexer-score.cu is NOT an R16 drift but a latent R12 defect (b1b0fa807): the
  fused GGML_OP_INDEXER_SCORE node called ggml_rope_get_truncate(dst), and upstream's #30206 added an
  assert that the argument is a ROPE/ROPE_BACK node.  Every qwen4exp sparse QSA decode run has
  aborted on this tree since R12 (no R12-R15 gate reaches that arm -- the coherence arms and both
  qwen4exp gates run the dense arm; block 15's residency gate reaches it because its `pref` arm sets
  LLAMA_QSA_DENSE_DECODE_UNTIL=0, and aborted after 63 generated tokens at ggml.c:4648).  Both call
  sites now pass /*truncate*/ true, which is the graph's own rope node default (ggml_rope_impl
  initialises no_trunc 0 and nothing calls ggml_rope_set_truncate on the indexer-key node) and the
  pre-#30206 5-argument helper's unconditional floor/ceil, i.e. pre-re-base numerics.

Coherence (same session, same commands, this build family): dense 4B 1de99b7e6ee6, 30B-A3B
4b4d56191368, 35B-A3B 3 GPU tensor rccl 86b7f9b5aa80, Flash-Next GSQ 7a8734a9f1a6 -- all four
unchanged from R13.

Gates:
* gate-kv-residency.sh PASS.  Window: wref == wres == wspill be904e86f248, wres 0 flips / 0 MiB
  host-backed, wspill 16 flips / 64 MiB, every slide on the map grid.  Pool: pref == pres == pfloor
  f260d1824ab3, bad 0, 8192 pages (408.0 MiB) on pres vs 4104 (204.4 MiB) on pfloor, 252 resolves
  both, claims 137.7 -> 217.1 per resolve, hits 91.02 -> 89.63 %.  Multi-device (-sm layer 0,1):
  pmref == pmres == pmfloor f260d1824ab3, one mirror/pool/counter block per device, 2 counter blocks
  summed, 117.8 -> 268.1 claims per resolve.
* gate-kv-window-split.sh PASS, 38/38: one region per device on a 3-device 4B, a 27B at -c 524288
  sliding on BOTH devices (32 flips each), -c 1048576 windowed, 1-device unchanged, -nkvo still
  declines, all five fit arms (fixed/auto/ram/ram-drop/off), and win2mtp == ref2mtp with identical
  acceptance 0.46154 whose batched state save takes the region path.
* gate-spec-draft-window.sh PASS: LLAMA_SPEC_DRAFT_WINDOW=1024 gives "1024 cells per sequence, cache
  3072 cells ((win + 512) x 2)" and all six requests across both slots are byte-identical to win 0,
  acceptance identical (0.47222 / 17-36, 1.0 / 23-23).
* check-gpu-faults.sh --since the session start: clean.

r247 (issue #293 follow-up): all three placements default OFF, and the pool stops being a size knob.

The MTP draft window shipped with `auto` as its default from r246 and that cost MTP decode whenever the
request was deeper than the window: measured -9.7 % on a `-sm tensor` split at ~105k tokens (65 536-cell
`auto` window 72.7 t/s against 80.5 off; text byte-identical; benchmarks/mtp-draft-window-depth.md).
`--spec-draft-kv-window` now defaults to 0 in BOTH `common_params` and `llama_context_params`, and `auto`
(cap or nothing) / `N` stay exactly as r246 defined them, as a conscious opt-in.

The three placements now read the same way -- default off, `auto` = the system picks, `N` = explicit:
  * `--spec-draft-kv-window [auto|N]`  (default 0)  truncates the DRAFTER's cache; lossy, measured caveat
  * `--kv-window [auto|N]`             (default 0)  the LOSSLESS resident window, promoted from the
    LLAMA_KV_RESIDENT_CELLS env var, which stays as the option's deprecated alias (the fit path and every
    shipped script keep working).  New `llama_context_params.kv_resident_cells`
  * `--kv-attendance-pool [on|off]`    (default off) the host-mirror + device page cache, renamed from
    `--kv-region-pool` (kept as an alias).  Its SIZE is no longer a knob: it is derived from the model
    (one decode band of the indexer working set, `QSA_DECODE_BAND x ceil(top_k / page)`), because a numeric
    request only ever bought ~1 point of hit rate for 2x the VRAM and `auto` had nothing to size it
    (TODO #313, closed).  A legacy numeric size or `auto` is accepted and IGNORED, with a WARN saying so.

Default-OFF is what makes the window's cost a documented caveat instead of a shipped regression, and it
also means no default run carries a placement decision at all.

TODO #314 (r247): --fit now NAMES the placements and takes neither.  With every block-15 placement off by
default, a config that no longer fits had no hint at all.  The fit's "does NOT fit" ERROR block lists
`--kv-window N` and `--kv-attendance-pool` with their measured costs (11-26 % of decode past the window's
depth; ~-48 % of prompt throughput for the pool) and says they are alternatives, skipping whichever is already
active; the fit's exception path prints the same block as a WARN, once per fit.  It takes NOTHING on the
user's behalf -- a placement chosen for the user is exactly the r246 -> r247 regression.

Also fixes a pre-existing units bug in the line above it: `ctx_mib` is a BYTE count, so the per-1024-token
figure printed 67721728 instead of 64.  The byte figure is kept (so the token estimate, whose units cancelled,
is unchanged) and divided by MiB only for display.
